{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518753-marking-territory-or-alternatives-to-pissing-all-over-the-place","id":518753,"title":"Marking Territory, or Alternatives to Pissing All Over The Place","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-18T20:12:56-07:00","id":518753,"title":"Marking Territory, or Alternatives to Pissing All Over The Place","content":"I suppose the topic title should explain it.<br /> <br /> How does your pack, or if you're not playing, how do you imagine your pack would mark their territory? Alternatively if you're an idea person and thought of interesting ways for it to be handled, share it here. I'm particularly interested in how you think Iron Masters or other more technologically inclined packs might manage it.<br /> <br /> I believe in first edition we had a sort of rite that allowed us to mark certain objects within the territory to form a border. And in second we do have a rite that sort of establishes a hunting ground and territory, but doesn't necessarily leave a trace behind, though the sample rite suggests it should. 'Many packs in Britain follow the tradition of beating the bounds. They travel around the border of the territory on foot, striking boundary markers with staves bearing the markings of their pack and totem. Great gouges that mark corner-stones and ancient tree trunks are clear indications of old territories.' A lot of the examples in first edition seemed to go with the vampire method, with graffiti or certain symbols of ownership carved into walls or sprayed on street signs and benches.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T20:28:33-07:00","id":518795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518753-marking-territory-or-alternatives-to-pissing-all-over-the-place#post518753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the topic title should explain it.<br /> <br /> How does your pack, or if you're not playing, how do you imagine your pack would mark their territory? Alternatively if you're an idea person and thought of interesting ways for it to be handled, share it here. I'm particularly interested in how you think Iron Masters or other more technologically inclined packs might manage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Masters or other packs would have a handy tech spirit spit out a nice little text message would basically consists of &quot;You're in our land&quot; upon crossing the border combined with traffic light slowly turning to keep an eye on you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T22:18:18-07:00","id":518931,"title":"","content":"Have fun paying the spirits to do that. I'll just leave various bits of graffiti and markings, depending on the environment. Preferably in prior trespassers' blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T01:52:22-07:00","id":519121,"title":"","content":"Seems simple enough to allow Spirits allied with you to feed off of Loci in your territory. Basically showing that working with you has solid benefits. Also, plain ol' Gathra and social maneuvering to get them into your good graces in the first place. <br /> <br /> Second Edition has a funny fluff thing on one page where a Pack leaves flyers around their territory going &quot;Missing: Five Wolfhounds. If found contact Luna.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T06:54:33-07:00","id":519515,"title":"","content":"We used a combination of Rites and physical markings, and then had a pact with the Spirits (Wind/Ravens) of the city to alert us to the intrusion of non-Pack Werewolves. Worked out pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:22:13-07:00","id":519682,"title":"","content":"My Pack uses graffiti and my gossip spirit pal, Twitter. Twitter doesn't pose a threat, or do anything useful, it just a stream of consciousness, rapid fire conversation that annoys Uratha and Pure who wander into the territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:44:13-07:00","id":519890,"title":"","content":"In second edition? Warding Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:55:48-07:00","id":519917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518753-marking-territory-or-alternatives-to-pissing-all-over-the-place?p=519890#post519890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In second edition? Warding Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work? Do you have a really small territory? Or a great surplus of essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:11:44-07:00","id":519944,"title":"","content":"Even a lvl 1 locus can support one or two of the wisdom facets, among the whole territory. Set one for werewolves, set another spirits getting to twilight. Alternatively, hunt a rank 1 spirit, get 5+ essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T03:02:32-07:00","id":524196,"title":"","content":"In our game the pack uses clawmarks on trees, and pawprints on stones that emit a spiritual signature that tresspassers are on someones elses turf.<br /> If they get closer (they have a lot of turf nowadays) flocks of crows or ravens will start to follow them around, harassing and bothering the invaders.<br /> The pack will also be alerted by ravens or crows about the trespassers.<br /> <br /> Since they host a protectorate in their territory this has led to some large flocks of crows and ravens at times.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T11:44:31-07:00","id":524600,"title":"","content":"Creepy dolls made of twigs and animal bones hung from low branches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:17:01-07:00","id":524618,"title":"","content":"A lot of pretty cool ideas. I especially like tasking spirits and actual animals to help out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:56:02-07:00","id":534790,"title":"","content":"Spirits who help watch your borders don't have to be paid in Essence. They could be paid in the elimination of competing spirits, which just so happen to be the ones less cooperative to the local pack. <br /> <br /> In one part of our game, our protagonist pack claimed territory that had been zoned into high-tax oblivion by finnagling an exemption from the taxes. So their territorial claim was assisted by the zoning board and city council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:04:31-07:00","id":535730,"title":"","content":"First and foremost I would say you mark it by patrolling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}